[
  {
    "document": "policy.md",
    "fact": "Travel expenses in USD are approved when amount_usd is at or below the applicable limit, otherwise rejected. All amounts are whole dollars. Cite R_BASE and the city row.",
    "id": "R_BASE",
    "section": "1. Expense eligibility",
    "when": {}
  },
  {
    "document": "policy.md",
    "fact": "FIELD travel uses the lower of the city limit and 150 USD. Cite R_DEPARTMENT as well.",
    "id": "R_DEPARTMENT",
    "section": "9. Department budgets",
    "when": {
      "department": "FIELD"
    }
  },
  {
    "document": "controls.md",
    "fact": "A restricted vendor must be rejected even during an emergency. Retain the applicable limit and cite R_VENDOR and all rules used to establish that limit.",
    "id": "R_VENDOR",
    "section": "3. Vendor screening",
    "when": {
      "vendor_status": "restricted"
    }
  },
  {
    "document": "exceptions.md",
    "fact": "An emergency with an incident_id replaces the city and department limits with 1000 USD. Cite R_EMERGENCY, R_BASE, the city row, and R_DEPARTMENT if FIELD. Vendor controls still apply.",
    "id": "R_EMERGENCY",
    "section": "Appendix Q. Incident travel",
    "when": {
      "emergency": true
    }
  },
  {
    "document": "policy.md",
    "fact": "Before applying any other rule, abstain with null limit and cite only R_ABSTAIN if city has no lookup row, category is not travel, currency is not USD, amount_usd is missing or is not a nonnegative integer, department is not OFFICE or FIELD, vendor_status is not clear or restricted, emergency is missing or not boolean, emergency is true without incident_id, or receipt_amount_usd is present and differs from amount_usd. Missing city, category, currency, department, or vendor_status also requires abstention.",
    "id": "R_ABSTAIN",
    "section": "0. Evidence completeness",
    "when": {}
  },
